{"title":"Distinct lines","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span id=\"What_Is_A_Distinct_Line.3F\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"What_Is_A_Distinct_Line?\">What Is A Distinct Line?</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct_lines&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: What Is A Distinct Line?\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Distinct lines are two or more lines that intersect at one point or less. This means that they cannot have the same equation. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_Of_A_Problem_Using_Distinct_Lines\">Example Of A Problem Using Distinct Lines</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct_lines&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Example Of A Problem Using Distinct Lines\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many distinct lines can you draw on a 5x5 grid that intersect at least two points on the grid?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Follow_Up\">Follow Up</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct_lines&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Follow Up\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If anyone would like more information on distinct lines, please feel free to message me at @owlmathlove. I hope I helped!\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Distinct_lines&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017120740\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nCo